From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Martin Lund <mrlund@hotmail.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 12:16:18 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] power: reset: nvmem-reboot-mode: write only the bytes a cell
 holds

nvmem_reboot_mode_write() passed sizeof(unsigned int) to
nvmem_cell_write(). pmk8550's reboot-reason cell is one byte with a
bitfield, so the write returns -EINVAL. The reboot still happens,
and ABL sees no reason and starts the normal system.

On the OnePlus 13, reboot-to bootloader then returned to OxygenOS.
After writing the cell's own length, the same command landed in
fastboot (product sun, slot a) with no adb device.

Follows Jennifer Berringer's smaller-magic series, using
nvmem_cell_read() for the length so this tree does not need
nvmem_cell_size().
---
 drivers/power/reset/nvmem-reboot-mode.c | 19 +++++++++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 17 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/power/reset/nvmem-reboot-mode.c b/drivers/power/reset/nvmem-reboot-mode.c
index 41530b70c..75c60c422 100644
--- a/drivers/power/reset/nvmem-reboot-mode.c
+++ b/drivers/power/reset/nvmem-reboot-mode.c
@@ -10,6 +10,7 @@
 #include <linux/nvmem-consumer.h>
 #include <linux/platform_device.h>
 #include <linux/reboot-mode.h>
+#include <linux/slab.h>
 
 struct nvmem_reboot_mode {
 	struct reboot_mode_driver reboot;
@@ -19,12 +20,26 @@ struct nvmem_reboot_mode {
 static int nvmem_reboot_mode_write(struct reboot_mode_driver *reboot,
 				    unsigned int magic)
 {
-	int ret;
 	struct nvmem_reboot_mode *nvmem_rbm;
+	size_t buf_len;
+	void *buf;
+	int ret;
 
 	nvmem_rbm = container_of(reboot, struct nvmem_reboot_mode, reboot);
 
-	ret = nvmem_cell_write(nvmem_rbm->cell, &magic, sizeof(magic));
+	/*
+	 * pmk8550 stores the reason in a 1-byte SDAM cell. Writing
+	 * sizeof(magic) is rejected, and the reboot then happens with
+	 * no reason stored. Write only as many bytes as the cell holds.
+	 */
+	buf = nvmem_cell_read(nvmem_rbm->cell, &buf_len);
+	if (IS_ERR(buf))
+		return PTR_ERR(buf);
+	kfree(buf);
+	if (!buf_len || buf_len > sizeof(magic))
+		return -EINVAL;
+
+	ret = nvmem_cell_write(nvmem_rbm->cell, &magic, buf_len);
 	if (ret < 0)
 		dev_err(reboot->dev, "update reboot mode bits failed\n");
 
-- 
2.55.0

